# Frontend git workflow (published SPA in Bedrock)

Bedrock tracks **only** the Apache-served build under `web/frontend/`:

- Tracked: `index.html`, `favicon.svg`, `team-bg.*`, `assets/` (hashed bundles + fonts/images)
- Ignored: `src/`, Vite tooling, `node_modules/`, `dist/`

Source is the separate repo [ports-sacco-frontend](https://github.com/jkkenzie/ports-sacco-frontend), checked out as a **nested git repo** in `web/frontend/` (manual git there; not a Bedrock submodule).

## Source changes (ports-sacco-frontend)

```bash
cd web/frontend
# edit src/, commit/push to ports-sacco-frontend as usual
git add src ...
git commit -m "Describe source change"
git push origin main
```

## Publish into Bedrock (for server `git pull`)

```bash
cd web/frontend
npm run build          # vite → dist/ → publish into this folder (index.html, assets/)
cd ../..               # Bedrock root
git add web/frontend/index.html web/frontend/assets web/frontend/favicon.svg web/frontend/team-bg.png web/frontend/team-bg.svg
git commit -m "Update published SPA build"
git push origin main
```

Server: `git pull` only — no npm, no copy from `dist/`.
